 "brief": "Seiberg–Witten, Monopoles, duality and chiral symmetry breaking in N=2 supersymmetric QCD (1994) — exact metric on the moduli space of quantum vacua and exact stable-state spectrum for SU(2) with…",
 "extended": "**Monopoles, Duality and Chiral Symmetry Breaking in N=2 Supersymmetric QCD** — N. Seiberg and E. Witten. arXiv:hep-th/9408099, RU-94-60, IASSNS-HEP-94/55, 17 Aug 1994.\n\nFour-dimensional N=2 supersymmetric gauge theories with matter multiplets. For all such models with gauge group SU(2), derives the **exact** metric on the moduli space of quantum vacua and the **exact** spectrum of stable massive states, including the monopole/dyon states whose condensation drives confinement and chiral symmetry breaking.\n\n**Why it may bear here.** This is the second Seiberg–Witten paper — the origin of the exact-moduli-space / BPS-spectrum technology that the Stokes-constant and DT/BPS material in this corpus refers back to. Registered as a foundational source; no specific result here is claimed to be in use.",
 "tokens": {
